Suggested approach for Conduct a security review:
1. Implement the requirement in the named App Router convention or trusted server layer.
2. Add explicit input validation and a user-friendly empty/error/denied state.
3. Exercise the normal case and at least one boundary case.
4. Run lint/tests and a production build in the target Next.js version.

Starter to adapt:
const user = await verifySession();
if (!user) throw new Error('Authentication required');
if (!canEdit(user, resource)) throw new Error('Forbidden');

Required static markers: verifySession, canEdit, Forbidden. These only provide a limited automatic signal; acceptance criteria must be manually reviewed.
